# A Laboratory Application of Microcomputer Graphics.

**Authors:** Gehring, Kalle B., Moore, John W.

## Abstract
A PASCAL graphics and instrument interface program for a Z80/S-100 based microcomputer was developed. The computer interfaces to a stopped-flow spectrophotometer replacing a storage oscilloscope and polaroid camera. Applications of this system are discussed, indicating that graphics and analog-to-digital boards have transformed the computer into an advanced digital storage oscilloscope. (JN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ281717

